{"id":19859,"path":"/grammar-points/a2/verbs-with-two-objects/","parentId":542,"order":280,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a2","depth":3,"title":"Verbs with two objects","seo":{"title":"Verbs with two objects - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use verbs with two objects correctly. Check our grammar explanation and grammar chart, and then do three different exercises!","image":"/media/uploads/verbs-with-two-objects.jpg"},"modified":"2026-02-25T08:34:59","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct options to complete these sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"721\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct options to complete these sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"722\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Rewrite these sentences using the structure verb + direct object + <em>to</em> or <em>for</em> + indirect object.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: I sent my friends a picture. ⇒ I sent <span class=\"textGap\">a picture to my friends</span>.</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"723\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2>Verbs with two objects: Grammar chart</h2> <p><img class=\"alignleft size-full wp-image-19898\" src=\"/media/uploads/Verbs-with-two-objects.png\" alt=\"Verbs with two objects - double object verbs\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h2>Direct and indirect objects</h2> <p>The direct object typically answers the question of ‘what’ or ‘who’.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I bought <strong><span>a nice sweater</span></strong>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>What</strong></span> did you buy?</em></li> <li><em>I saw <span><strong>Peter and Sarah</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Who</strong></span> did you see?</em></li> </ul> <p>The indirect object typically answers the question ‘to whom’ or ‘for whom’.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I sent <span><strong>my friends</strong></span> a picture of the house.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Who</strong></span> did you send a picture <span><strong>to</strong></span>?</em></li> <li><em>I cooked my wife breakfast.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Who</strong></span> did you cook breakfast <span><strong>for</strong></span>?</em></li> </ul> <h2>Verbs with two objects</h2> <p>There are some verbs which have two objects: an indirect object and a direct object.<br> <br> Some of these verbs are:</p> <div class=\"textBox\"><strong>bring, buy, cook, find, get, give, lend, make, offer, pass, promise, read, sell, send, show, tell,</strong> and <strong>write</strong>.</div> <p> After these verbs, there are two possible structures:</p> <div class=\"infoblock\"> <p>‣ I sent <span class=\"highYellow\">my friends</span> <span class=\"highBlue\">a picture</span>.</p> <p>‣ I sent <span class=\"highBlue\">a picture</span> <span class=\"highYellow\">to my friends</span>.</p> </div> <p>If the indirect object is a , we normally use it next to the verb.</p> <div class=\"infoblock\"> <p>‣ I sent <span class=\"highYellow\">them</span> <span class=\"highBlue\">a picture</span>.</p> </div> <p></p> <h4><strong>To</strong> or <strong>for</strong>?</h4> <p>When we use the indirect object next to the verb, we do not use <strong>to</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>for</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I send <span><strong>to Alex</strong></span> a postcard. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I send <span><strong>Alex</strong></span> a postcard.</em> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>to</strong> or <strong>for</strong> in: verb + direct object + <strong>to/for </strong>+ indirect object.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I sent a postcard <span><strong>to</strong></span> Alex.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>She bought a present <span><strong>for</strong></span> her friend.</em></li> </ul> <p>Some verbs are used with <strong>to</strong>, and some other verbs are used with <strong>for</strong> before the indirect object.</p> <h4><strong>To</strong> + indirect object</h4> <p>Some common verbs that are used with&nbsp;<strong>to&nbsp;</strong>+ indirect object are <strong>give, lend, offer, pass, promise, read, sell, send, show, tell,</strong> and <strong>write</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>You should give an apology <strong><span>to</span></strong> Tom.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>She showed the letter <span><strong>to</strong></span> all her friends.</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>For</strong> + indirect object</h4> <p>Some common verbs that are used with&nbsp;<strong>for </strong>+ indirect object are <strong>bring, buy, cook, find, get,</strong> and <strong>make</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Can you bring some food <span><strong>for</strong></span> the dog?</em></li> <li><em>I’ll cook a nice dinner <strong><span>for</span></strong> you.</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":721,"questions":[{"id":6170,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I sent <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a postcard. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["him","for her","to me"]}]},{"id":6171,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I wrote a letter <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["to him","for him","him"]}]},{"id":6172,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Have you brought <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["me a cake","a cake me","a cake to me"]}]},{"id":6173,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They offered <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["to me a discount","me a discount","a discount me"]}]},{"id":6174,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Pass <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>, please.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["our guest the biscuits","the biscuits our guest","to our guest the biscuits"]}]},{"id":6175,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She made <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["a bracelet for her sister","a bracelet to her sister","to her sister a bracelet"]}]},{"id":6176,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She taught <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a lesson.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["me","to me","for me"]}]},{"id":6177,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I cooked <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["some pasta for the children","for the children some pasta","some pasta to the children"]}]},{"id":6178,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I never lend <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["money anyone","anyone money","to anyone money"]}]},{"id":6179,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If you have any questions, give <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["to me a call","me a call","a call me"]}]}]},{"id":722,"questions":[{"id":6180,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He showed _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10558,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the police a video of the robbers.</span>"},{"id":10559,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to the police a video of the robbers.</span>"},{"id":10560,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>a video of the robbers for the police</span>"}]},{"id":6181,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They promised _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10561,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to their daughter a new car</span>"},{"id":10562,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>a new car their daughter</span>"},{"id":10563,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>their daughter a new car</span>"}]},{"id":6182,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We should get ______ for her birthday.</div>","choices":[{"id":10564,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>her a present</span>"},{"id":10565,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>a present her</span>"},{"id":10566,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>for her a present</span>"}]},{"id":6183,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They found _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10567,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>a place to stay me</span>"},{"id":10568,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>me a place to stay</span>"},{"id":10569,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>to me a place to stay</span>"}]},{"id":6184,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She gave ______.</div>","choices":[{"id":10570,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to the waiter a generous tip</span>"},{"id":10571,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the waiter a generous tip</span>"},{"id":10572,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>a generous tip the waiter</span>"}]},{"id":6185,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You should tell _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10573,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to the police the truth</span>"},{"id":10574,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the police the truth</span>"},{"id":10575,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the truth for the police</span>"}]},{"id":6186,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He reads _____ every night.</div>","choices":[{"id":10576,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>them a story </span>"},{"id":10577,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to them a story</span>"},{"id":10578,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>a story them</span>"}]},{"id":6187,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She brought _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10579,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>a cake me</span>"},{"id":10580,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>for me a cake</span>"},{"id":10581,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>a cake for me</span>"}]},{"id":6188,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He has offered _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10582,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to his brother a job</span>"},{"id":10583,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>a job his brother</span>"},{"id":10584,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>a job to his brother</span>"}]},{"id":6189,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Send _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10585,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>a copy them</span>"},{"id":10586,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to them a copy</span>"},{"id":10587,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>them a copy</span>"}]}]},{"id":723,"questions":[{"id":6197,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She wrote her father a long email. ⇒ She wrote <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6193,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Did you buy the children a present? ⇒ Did you buy <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6190,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He gave the clerk his card. ⇒ He gave <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6191,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I offered the police officer a drink. ⇒ I offered <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6192,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I made my wife a cake. ⇒ I made <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6195,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He sold his neighbour his apartment. ⇒ He sold <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6196,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He lent me some money. ⇒ He lent <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6194,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She sent her sister a letter. ⇒ She sent <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6198,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She read the audience a message. ⇒ She read <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":6199,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He showed the doctor his arm. ⇒ He showed <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}